   "title": "How to use",
   "properties": {
    "widget_ue_connectable": {}
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Qwen-Image-2.1 image edit \u00b7 up to 4 reference pictures\n\nMain image + up to 3 references, and one sentence of instruction does the edit.\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. \"Main image\" is required \u2014 the picture being edited (the client).\n2. \"Reference 1 / 2 / 3\" are optional \u2014 use them to swap clothing, background or style.\n3. \"Edit instruction\" is the sentence that says what to change. Name the pictures:\n   \"<Picture 1>\" is the main image, \"<Picture 2>\" is the first reference, and so on.\n4. The frame is 1024 px on the short side; set width/height on the encoder if you need another ratio.\n\nKEEP IT IN ONE FRAME\nDescribe the finished photograph, not a list of pictures. \"The person in <Picture 1>\nwearing the coat from <Picture 2>\" produces one image; a list of labelled references\ntends to produce a grid of separate panels."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "Qwen-Image-2.1 image edit \u00b7 up to 4 reference pictures\n\nMain image + up to 3 references, and one sentence of instruction does the edit.\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. \"Main image\" is required \u2014 the picture being edited (the client).\n2. \"Reference 1 / 2 / 3\" are optional \u2014 use them to swap clothing, background or style.\n3. \"Edit instruction\" is the sentence that says what to change. Name the pictures:\n   \"<Picture 1>\" is the main image, \"<Picture 2>\" is the first reference, and so on.\n4. The frame is 1024 px on the short side; set width/height on the encoder if you need another ratio.\n\nKEEP IT IN ONE FRAME\nDescribe the finished photograph, not a list of pictures. \"The person in <Picture 1>\nwearing the coat from <Picture 2>\" produces one image; a list of labelled references\ntends to produce a grid of separate panels."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
